Original commit body from 1ab7ff7:

Three fixes for entrypoint detection issues discovered in socketio-chat-example:

1. Case-insensitive HTTP method matching: The JS/TS analyzer stores
   uppercase HTTP methods (GET, POST) in stable_id, but the entrypoint
   detector compared against lowercase HTTP_ROUTE_DECORATORS. Now uses
   case-insensitive matching.

2. Metadata-based route detection: Added fallback detection for routes
   with meta.http_method set (Express inline handlers like
   `app.get('/', (req, res) => {})`).

3. Full analyzer support in slice: Changed `hypergumbo slice --entry auto`
   to use run_all_analyzers() instead of only Python/HTML. This ensures
   JS/TS routes are detected when running slice without a pre-existing
   hypergumbo.results.json file.

4. Metadata preservation: Fixed _node_from_dict to preserve the meta
   field when reconstructing symbols from JSON.
